# Pantomina — Input bounds

All form clamps go through `Pantomina/Engine/InputBounds.swift`. UI does not invent parallel limits.

## Wiring

| Field kind | Live typing | On save / commit |
|---|---|---|
| Person / fund / Keep Doing titles | `limiting(_:max: maxDisplayNameLength)` | `clampDisplayName` |
| Pet names | `limiting` + `maxPetNameLength` | `clampPetName` |
| Notes (Add, jar, borrow, journal, …) | `clampNote` via `onChange` | `clampNote` then trim |
| Money (peso text) | optional | `centavos(fromPesosText:)` / `isValidAmountC` |
| Snowball order / batch | number pad | `clampQueueIndex` — empty order → `nil`; batch when shown must parse |

## Do not

- Ship a new `TextField` without matching the table above.
- Hard-code 40 / 24 / 200 / 100M / 99 in views — use `InputBounds` constants.
- Reimplement parse/clamp in the view layer.
